cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DVAH — Damn Vulnerable Agent Harness"
message: "If you use DVAH in research or training, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Avishay
    family-names: Bar
    website: "https://avishay.co.il"
repository-code: "https://github.com/avishayil/dvah"
url: "https://avishay.co.il"
abstract: >-
  DVAH is a patch-the-runtime security lab for AI-agent platforms. Learners exploit
  architectural failures in an intentionally-insecure agent runtime, trace them, identify
  the broken security invariant, patch the harness, and prove the fix holds against an
  adversarial test suite. It is organized around durable security invariants rather than
  vulnerability names.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - security
  - agent-security
  - security-training
  - invariants
  - mcp
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
